    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0907" n="847" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg847"/>

                <head>Mr. Hovey to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 114.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Lima, Peru,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-01-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 28, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> On the 22d instant General Pedro Diez
                    Canseco arrived at this city, and immediately proceeded to take charge of the
                    government. On the 25th the new cabinet was organized as follows: Minister of
                    foreign affairs, Don Juan M. Polar; minister of interior, Don Antonio Arenas;
                    minister of finance and president of the council, Don J. Luis Gomez Sanchez;
                    minister of justice, Don Bernardo Munoz; minister of war and marine, General
                    Fernando Alvizuri.</p>
                <p>I have not yet been informed officially of the existence of this cabinet.</p>
                <p>The country appears to be tranquil, and, as well as can be learned of the public
                    feeling, it seems to be in favor of the new order of things.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALVIN P. HOVEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
